<title>SWEDEN: Swedish Fin Min says no plans to link crown to ERM.</title>
<headline>Swedish Fin Min says no plans to link crown to ERM.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's Finance Minister Erik Asbrink said on Tuesday there were no plans to link the crown to Europe's exchange rate mechanism (ERM). &quot;Linking the crown to ERM, or to ERM2, is not on the agenda,&quot; Asbrink told reporters following the ruling party's annoucement that it would not join Europe's economic and monetary union (EMU) at the euro's planned 1999 start.</p>
<p>A link to ERM2 would only become an issue if Sweden decided to join EMU, Asbrink said.</p>
<p>-- Peter Fellman, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1016</p>
</text>
